<body>

    <header>
        <h1>🏸 All About Badminton</h1>
        <p>A fast-paced sport that combines speed, skill and strategy!</p>
    </header>

    <nav>
        <a href="#about">About</a>
        <a href="#equipment">Equipment</a>
        <a href="#rules">Rules</a>
        <a href="#benefits">Benefits</a>
    </nav>

    <main>

        <section id="about">
            <h2>What is Badminton?</h2>
            <p>
                Badminton is a racket sport played by either two players
                (singles) or four players (doubles). Players hit a shuttlecock
                over a net, trying to make it land inside their opponent's court.
            </p>
            <p>
                It is an Olympic sport that requires quick reactions,
                coordination, agility and tactical thinking.
            </p>
            <div class="highlight">
                <strong>Did you know?</strong>
                The shuttlecock is designed to create significant air resistance,
                which makes it slow down rapidly after being hit.
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="equipment">
            <h2>Essential Equipment</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>🏸 Racket — used to hit the shuttlecock.</li>
                <li>🪶 Shuttlecock — the object players hit across the net.</li>
                <li>🥾 Court shoes — provide grip and support.</li>
                <li>👕 Sportswear — comfortable clothing for movement.</li>
                <li>🏟️ Net and court — define the playing area.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="rules">
            <h2>Basic Rules</h2>
            <ol>
                <li>A match is normally played as the best of three games.</li>
                <li>Each game is played to 21 points.</li>
                <li>A rally earns a point for the player or pair that wins it.</li>
                <li>A player must hit the shuttlecock over the net and into the court.</li>
                <li>The shuttlecock is out if it lands outside the relevant court boundaries.</li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <section id="benefits">
            <h2>Why Play Badminton?</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Improves cardiovascular fitness.</li>
                <li>Develops hand-eye coordination.</li>
                <li>Builds agility and reaction speed.</li>
                <li>Encourages teamwork and communication.</li>
                <li>Provides a fun way to socialise.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>Made by a badminton enthusiast 🏸</p>
    </footer>

